## PROPRIETARY & CLOSED-SOURCE NOTICE: OBSX SENTINEL™

The **OBSX Sentinel™ Adaptive Vector Circuit Breaker Engine** (autonomous vector isolation, distributed zero-day threat correlation, dynamic saturation throttling, real-time edge heuristics, and vector state machines) is **STRICTLY CLOSED SOURCE AND PROPRIETARY INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY**.

- **Not Included in this Repository:** Sentinel™ is **NOT** included in this public repository and is **NOT** licensed under the MIT License or the Elastic License 2.0.
- **Private Repository & Cloud Exclusive:** Sentinel™ is maintained exclusively in a private, proprietary repository (`jidiotspam-hue/obsx-sentinel`) under the *OBSX Sentinel™ Enterprise Proprietary Software License* and is deployed exclusively as a managed service powering the official cloud platform at **https://obsx.tech**.
- **Strict Prohibition on Emulation, Shimming & Clean-Room Replication:** You may **NOT** decompile, reverse-engineer, clean-room implement, emulate, shim, or duplicate the Sentinel™ architecture, algorithms, interface contracts, vector classifications, or methods, nor create drop-in replacement modules or shims purporting to substitute for or replicate OBSX Sentinel™. The MIT license covering Zone 1 applies solely to the standalone core protocol engine operating in baseline open-source mode and explicitly **DOES NOT** grant any right to recreate, shim, or simulate Sentinel™.
- **Self-Hosting Independence:** Self-hosted deployments from this repository execute the complete, fully functional, zero-dependency OBSX Core verification engine (Zone 1) with operator scaffolding (Zone 2) in baseline open-source mode.

